@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] settings-show-what-you-choose
Where a setting changes how something looks, the control is the thing itself as a small
sample: the diff layout is two small diffs, the code size is three sizes over a line of
code that resizes, and each code font is set in its own face (rule 81; F12).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-more-than-three-is-a-page
A choice of more than three options (Code font, Model, the button sound) is a row with
the chosen one on its right that opens a page inside the Settings sheet, with a tick on
the chosen one (rule 126; J5).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-sound-pick-plays-it
Picking a button sound plays one cue in it and goes back. Nothing explains the sounds,
on or off (rule 126; J4).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-vibration-switch
Settings, Sounds has a Vibration switch, and with it off nothing vibrates (rule 109; H18).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-server-is-advanced
The server address, the Access token, Past versions and the UI Book sit under an
Advanced row at the bottom of Settings, not on its main page (H9).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-model-row-names-the-model
The Model row shows the chosen model's name and the engine's own mark in colour, never a
model ID and never a robot icon (rules 48 and 89; H7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-no-helper-lines
Settings carries no lines that explain its rows ("Claude Code and Codex run on this
machine...", "The server uses its own GitHub sign-in...", "Pulls asks your server for a
new version..."): "These are just unnecessary straight up" (H8).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-is-the-liked-sheet
Settings is a sheet in the mobile style, with its pages inside it. Tavi called it "much,
much better than before"; it MUST NOT regress to the old style (rules 49 and 78; F11).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-past-versions-slider
Settings, Advanced, Past versions has a dev-only slider over every version of the app,
oldest on the left. It rests on the running version, so the app MUST always run the
newest UI unless an older one is opened from there. An older version opens as that
version's own build from git, beside this app, never as a mode of this one (Tavi,
15 Oct: "a dev-only slider ... by default the app just has latest changes"). While the
server has built none yet the page says so and that it builds them after each update,
newest first; only a failed request says the server could not be reached (recording
16 Oct 09:50, 01:09 to 01:14; M3).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] settings-effort-under-model
Settings has an Effort row of its own right under Model whenever the chosen model has
more than one effort, and the model list has no effort at its bottom, so nobody scrolls
past every model to reach it. The Analyze sheet shows Effort the same way ("put effort as
an option here", recording 16 Oct 09:50, 00:44 to 01:04; M2).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] settings-usage-stats-drops-queue
The main Settings page has a Usage stats switch, on by default, with a Stats row beside
it that opens Settings, Stats. Turning it off MUST drop every queued event, in memory and
on disk, cancel the job waiting to send them, and track nothing more until it is turned
on again; the turning off itself is not sent. While it is off, Stats says so instead of
asking the server (message 15 Oct 20:58 and 21:12; plan "Pulls analytics on our own
server", Guardrails).
